===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|snuor|g=f}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|snuor}}. Originally a neuter, nevertheless still cognate with {{cog|nl|snoer}}, {{cog|en|snare}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Schnüre}}

# [[cord]], [[string]]
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[cable]] {{gloss|electronic wire}}

=====Usage notes=====
* A ''Schnur'' is thicker than a {{m|de|Faden||thread}}, but thinner than a {{m|de|Seil||rope}}.

=====Declension=====
{{de-decl-noun-f|pl=Schnüre}}

